  "final": "`get_document` and `list_documents` now only return documents that match both the tenant and the owner and have `deleted_at IS NULL`. `python3 checks/public.py` passes, including the new checks I added.\n\n- **`src/repository.py`:** `find` and `listing` now take `tenant` and `owner` and filter on `id`, `tenant`, `owner` and `deleted_at IS NULL`. Every value is passed as a bound parameter, so names containing quotes work and injection-style input matches nothing. Lists are ordered by `id`. Results are still dictionaries with only `id`, `title` and `body`.\n- **`src/service.py`:** both functions now pass `tenant` and `owner` through to the repository. `get_document` returns `None` for any ID that isn't available, so a missing, cross-tenant, cross-owner or deleted record looks the same to the caller.\n- **`checks/public.py`:** I added checks for these cases:\n  - cross-tenant, cross-owner and deleted IDs return `None`;\n  - lists are ordered by `id`;\n  - tenant and owner names containing quotes work;\n  - an injection-style tenant string returns an empty list.\n\n`find` and `listing` changed signature (they take `tenant`). I only looked at `src/` and `checks/`, so any other caller of them would need updating.\n\nThe sandbox has no `python` command, so I ran everything with `python3`.",
